# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source corpus — kept locally, never published
#
# These directories hold text extracted from commercially published,
# copyrighted books (Essential Linux Device Drivers, Professional Linux Kernel
# Architecture, Linux Kernel Development, Mastering Embedded Linux Programming,
# and others). They are working material for writing the notes in docs/ — they
# are not ours to redistribute, so they stay out of the repository.
#
# Note that a `.md` extension does not change this: the chunked `*_parts/`
# files are the same verbatim book text under a different suffix.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

RefManagement/
Learning-Path/
Linux/References/

# Chunked book extracts, wherever they appear
*_parts/
*_parts_txt/

# Raw extracted text
*.txt
!Linux/Kernel/PROGRESS.txt
!Linux/Kernel/PROJECT_COMPLETION_SUMMARY.txt
!Linux/Kernel/BOOK_TO_CHEATSHEET_MAPPING.txt
!Linux/Kernel/DETAILED_CROSSREFERENCE.txt

# Source documents
*.pdf
*.epub
*.chm
*.mobi
*.djvu
*:Zone.Identifier

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
site/
.cache/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ── Editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
